WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:02.201
-The weirdos,

00:00:02.201 --> 00:00:03.435
the many weirdos who tried

00:00:03.435 --> 00:00:05.972
to help Donald Trump
overthrow the election are

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:08.375
in major legal
and financial trouble.

00:00:08.375 --> 00:00:10.242
Trump is refusing
to help Rudy Giuliani

00:00:10.242 --> 00:00:11.244
pay his legal bills

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:13.747
and MyPillow CEO Mike Lindell,

00:00:13.747 --> 00:00:15.848
who's also been sued
for defamation,

00:00:15.848 --> 00:00:19.118
had yet another meltdown
at a so-called Cyber Symposium.

00:00:19.118 --> 00:00:21.287
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:21.287 --> 00:00:25.257
♪♪

00:00:25.257 --> 00:00:26.426
Before we get to all that,

00:00:26.426 --> 00:00:28.260
the big news in politics
right now, of course,

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:30.997
is the resignation of New York
Governor Andrew Cuomo,

00:00:30.997 --> 00:00:33.399
who's slinking away in disgrace
after a long run

00:00:33.399 --> 00:00:36.402
as one of the most corrupt
and cynical bullies in politics,

00:00:36.402 --> 00:00:40.206
not to mention the host of the
weirdest kids' show in history.

00:00:41.874 --> 00:00:43.175
[ Laughter ]
Thank you.

00:00:43.175 --> 00:00:45.311
Terrifying man.

00:00:45.311 --> 00:00:47.080
You know, it's hard to soothe
the soul of a nation

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:50.416
when you sound like
Chazz Palminteri's stuntman.

00:00:50.416 --> 00:00:52.251
[ Laughter ]
Anyway, a report
by the attorney general found

00:00:52.251 --> 00:00:54.220
that Cuomo sexually harassed
11 women.

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:56.388 line:0%
And let's not forget,
his administration also

00:00:56.388 --> 00:00:58.657 line:0%
covered up the COVID death toll
in nursing homes.

00:00:58.657 --> 00:01:00.259 line:0%
It's got to be the worst thing
he's covered up

00:01:00.259 --> 00:01:01.760 line:0%
since his nipples.

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:04.664
[ Laughter ]
I guess they also knew
how bad things were

00:01:04.664 --> 00:01:06.432
and they were trying
to get the hell out of there.

00:01:06.432 --> 00:01:09.002
[ Laughter ]
Those things like
porcupine quills.

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:11.637
They attack
when they're threatened.

00:01:11.637 --> 00:01:14.073
[ Laughter ]
Seriously, when even your
nipples are trying to escape,

00:01:14.073 --> 00:01:15.307
you know you're in a bad place.

00:01:15.307 --> 00:01:17.309
Maybe that's why he started
wearing a blanket,

00:01:17.309 --> 00:01:20.113
like he was just rescued
from the Miracle on the Hudson.

00:01:20.113 --> 00:01:21.447
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.447 --> 00:01:24.184
Look at him. Is he trying
to pull a "Mrs. Doubtfire"?

00:01:24.184 --> 00:01:25.985
I wouldn't be surprised
if Cuomo pretended

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:27.086
to be the British nanny

00:01:27.086 --> 00:01:29.121
so he could hang around
after he resigns.

00:01:29.121 --> 00:01:32.792
He just has to make sure he
doesn't also take his fake name

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:34.560
from the front page
of the newspaper.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:36.696
[ English accent ]
Oh, hello, my name is Mrs...

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:38.164
Andrew Cuomo.

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:40.533
[ Laughter ]
Oh, no, wait!
I mean, it's Mrs...

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:41.834
Disgraced Governor.

00:01:41.834 --> 00:01:43.269
Oh, dear.
Don't mind the nipples.

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:44.403
They're just frightened.

00:01:44.403 --> 00:01:45.505
[ Laughter ]
And when

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:47.306
he announced
his resignation yesterday,

00:01:47.306 --> 00:01:49.409
Cuomo tried to explain away
his actions

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:52.745
by claiming he didn't realize
he was doing anything wrong.

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:59.785
-In my mind, I've never crossed
the line with anyone.

00:01:59.785 --> 00:02:03.255
But, I didn't realize

00:02:03.255 --> 00:02:08.227
the extent to which
the line has been redrawn.

00:02:08.227 --> 00:02:10.195
-First of all, that's such
a ridiculous excuse.

00:02:10.195 --> 00:02:11.964
You're telling us
you didn't know

00:02:11.964 --> 00:02:13.199
what you were doing was wrong?

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:14.200
What's next,
you going to tell us

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:15.368
you didn't know what day it was?

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:17.871
You don't get to blame
the line for moving

00:02:17.871 --> 00:02:19.038
when you're the one
who crossed it.

00:02:19.038 --> 00:02:20.339
Although, I will say,
if you live in New York,

00:02:20.339 --> 00:02:21.673
you've probably heard
that before.

00:02:21.673 --> 00:02:24.076
Cuomo sounds like he's trying
to talk a traffic cop

00:02:24.076 --> 00:02:26.412
out of giving him a ticket
for parking in a fire lane.

00:02:26.412 --> 00:02:28.814
[ As Cuomo ]
I swear, when I parked,
the line was over here.

00:02:28.814 --> 00:02:29.882
Now you're telling me
it's over here?

00:02:29.882 --> 00:02:31.216
Come on,
you're breaking my balls!

00:02:31.216 --> 00:02:32.585
[ Laughter ]
It's a very

00:02:32.585 --> 00:02:35.154
George Costanza way of excusing
your [bleep] behavior.

00:02:35.154 --> 00:02:36.456
[ As Costanza ]
The line, Jerry, it moved!

00:02:36.456 --> 00:02:37.757
[ Laughter ]
They moved the line!

00:02:37.757 --> 00:02:39.325
Oh, it moved, baby!

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:41.394
[ Laughter ]
And it turned out I crossed it!

00:02:41.394 --> 00:02:42.394
[ As Seinfeld ]
You know what this means.

00:02:42.394 --> 00:02:43.630
You're a line-crosser.

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:44.730
[ As Costanza ]
Lines here, lines there!

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:46.232
I'm crossing lines all
over the place!

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:47.399
[ Laughter ]
[ As Elaine ] Have I

00:02:47.399 --> 00:02:49.502
got a line for you.

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:50.903
[ Laughter ]
[ As Seinfeld ]
Well, get in line!

00:02:50.903 --> 00:02:52.705
[ As Elaine ]
I was with Puddy last night

00:02:52.705 --> 00:02:54.040
and he used

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:55.341
the line.

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:56.776
[ As Seinfeld ]
He used the line?!

00:02:56.776 --> 00:02:58.578
[ As Costanza ]
I thought using the line
crossed the line!

00:02:58.578 --> 00:03:00.013
[ As Elaine ]
Not my line.

00:03:00.013 --> 00:03:03.048
[ As Seinfeld ]
Now, that's where I
draw the line.

00:03:03.048 --> 00:03:04.550
[ "Seinfeld" theme sting ]

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:09.689
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.689 --> 00:03:12.425
That camp was worth every penny.

00:03:12.425 --> 00:03:14.793
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.793 --> 00:03:17.997
So, obviously, this is not
how Andrew Cuomo planned

00:03:17.997 --> 00:03:19.365
to end his political career.

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:21.801
He was once the most
dominant, ruthless,

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:24.204
most Machiavellian force
in New York politics.

00:03:24.204 --> 00:03:26.205
Now, he's just the latest
in a long line

00:03:26.205 --> 00:03:27.907
of disgraced
New York politicians

00:03:27.907 --> 00:03:30.142
who will inevitably
get photographed

00:03:30.142 --> 00:03:31.344
by The New York Post

00:03:31.344 --> 00:03:33.879
with a long, scruffy beard
and a Mets hat,

00:03:33.879 --> 00:03:35.781
sloppily eating a dollar slice

00:03:35.781 --> 00:03:37.417
on a bench in Central Park
by himself.

00:03:37.417 --> 00:03:40.520
Central Park has a bench
specifically for that.

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:41.587
[ Laughter ]

00:03:41.587 --> 00:03:43.389
If only there were a way to,

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:44.590
I don't know, lift his spirits.

00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:46.859
Perhaps, I don't know,
a pep talk

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:49.495
from someone who knows
what he's going through.

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:52.431 line:0%
-Hi, it's Rudy Giuliani
and I'm on Cameo.

00:03:52.431 --> 00:03:54.667 line:0%
If there's an issue of concern
that you want to discuss

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:58.471 line:0%
or a story you'd like to hear
or share with me,

00:03:58.471 --> 00:04:00.973 line:0%
or a greeting
that I can bring to someone

00:04:00.973 --> 00:04:02.742
that would bring happiness
to their day,

00:04:02.742 --> 00:04:04.376
I would be delighted to do it.

00:04:04.376 --> 00:04:05.411
[ Chuckling ]
It can be arranged.

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:06.479
We can talk.

00:04:06.479 --> 00:04:07.913
Through the magic of Cameo.

00:04:07.913 --> 00:04:08.914
Thank you.

00:04:08.914 --> 00:04:10.950
-No, Rudy. Thank you.

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:12.751
I guess Rudy's last cameo
went so well,

00:04:12.751 --> 00:04:14.821
he decided to give it
another go.

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:15.921
[ Laughter ]
[ As Giuliani ]
For an extra 50 bucks,

00:04:15.921 --> 00:04:17.323
I'll tuck in my shirt.

00:04:17.323 --> 00:04:18.558
Also, where is he?

00:04:18.558 --> 00:04:20.726
Did he film that
in an IKEA showroom?

00:04:20.726 --> 00:04:22.594
Why does everything
looks so chintzy?

00:04:22.594 --> 00:04:24.964
Reminds me of action films
from the '80s

00:04:24.964 --> 00:04:26.432
where the characters
would be arguing

00:04:26.432 --> 00:04:28.934
in front of a set of shelves
that looked so cheap,

00:04:28.934 --> 00:04:31.337
you'd think,
"Oh, someone's definitely

00:04:31.337 --> 00:04:33.039
getting thrown into those."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:33.039 --> 00:04:34.173
Oh, Rudy.

00:04:34.173 --> 00:04:35.174
Sweet, sweet Rudy.

00:04:35.174 --> 00:04:36.809
He has no idea what he's in for.

00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:39.278
Right now, a prosecutor in the
Southern District of New York

00:04:39.278 --> 00:04:41.647
is logging on to Cameo
and asking Rudy

00:04:41.647 --> 00:04:43.783
to share the story of the time
he went to Ukraine

00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:45.918
to dig up dirt
on a political opponent

00:04:45.918 --> 00:04:47.820
to interfere
in a presidential election.

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:50.089
[ As Biden ]
This message is for Mr. DOJ.

00:04:50.089 --> 00:04:51.791
I hear you're feeling
discouraged at work.

00:04:51.791 --> 00:04:53.225
Well, let me tell you
about the time

00:04:53.225 --> 00:04:55.461
my friend Don and I
cooked up a scheme

00:04:55.461 --> 00:04:57.129
[ Laughter ]
to extort a foreign government

00:04:57.129 --> 00:04:58.330
and got away with it.

00:04:58.330 --> 00:05:00.066
Oh, it says here you want me
to read you

00:05:00.066 --> 00:05:02.502
my text messages and emails.

00:05:02.502 --> 00:05:05.004
Oh, hold on.
Someone's banging at the door.

00:05:05.004 --> 00:05:06.472
Why are you yelling "Police!"?

00:05:06.472 --> 00:05:07.673
There's no police in here.

00:05:07.673 --> 00:05:11.944
[ Laughter ]

00:05:11.944 --> 00:05:13.445
Now, Rudy's charging

00:05:13.445 --> 00:05:15.415
$275 per video.

00:05:15.415 --> 00:05:17.517
But, if you just wait a while,
you know,

00:05:17.517 --> 00:05:19.285
he'll eventually
butt-dial you for free.

00:05:19.285 --> 00:05:20.753
I mean, this guy,

00:05:20.753 --> 00:05:23.255
this guy,
who was the personal lawyer

00:05:23.255 --> 00:05:25.558
to the president
of the United States,

00:05:25.558 --> 00:05:27.293
and, now, he's basically
panhandling

00:05:27.293 --> 00:05:30.095
in the same place you can get
a "Happy Bat Mitzvah" message

00:05:30.095 --> 00:05:31.764
from Jamie Farr.
Does that count

00:05:31.764 --> 00:05:33.333
as a "M-A-S-H" reference?
You let us know.

00:05:33.333 --> 00:05:34.800
[ Laughter ]
Now, I will say it took

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:36.936
a lot of self-control
on our part

00:05:36.936 --> 00:05:39.905
not to buy a Cameo from Rudy
because, ultimately,

00:05:39.905 --> 00:05:41.473
even if you're doing it
as a joke,

00:05:41.473 --> 00:05:42.475
Rudy's still getting the money.

00:05:42.475 --> 00:05:43.642
It's not like it's joke money.

00:05:43.642 --> 00:05:44.910
I mean, Pizza Rat doesn't care

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:46.078
if the pizza's three days old.

00:05:46.078 --> 00:05:48.014
He's just happy he found
something to eat,

00:05:48.014 --> 00:05:49.581
especially something on-brand.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:49.581 --> 00:05:52.185
Plus, we don't have $275

00:05:52.185 --> 00:05:54.053
to throw away
on a dumb Cameo from Rudy

00:05:54.053 --> 00:05:56.622
because we have to keep paying
Wally for all his lines.

00:05:56.622 --> 00:06:00.326
In fact, Wally's so famous now,
he's doing his own Cameos.

00:06:00.326 --> 00:06:02.528
-Hey, this message is
for Rudy G.

00:06:02.528 --> 00:06:04.763
Keep going and don't let any
of those lame talk show hosts

00:06:04.763 --> 00:06:05.898
get you down, buddy.

00:06:05.898 --> 00:06:09.434
[ Laughter ]

00:06:09.434 --> 00:06:11.470
-You're very good at it, Wally.

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:12.738
-Thank you very much.
-You're very good.

00:06:12.738 --> 00:06:14.006
-Thank you.
[ Laughs ]

00:06:14.006 --> 00:06:16.509
[ Laughter ]
-And any money Rudy makes
from this

00:06:16.509 --> 00:06:19.111
will presumably go
toward paying the legal bills

00:06:19.111 --> 00:06:21.947
he's racked up from trying
to dig up dirt on Joe Biden

00:06:21.947 --> 00:06:23.982
and trying to overthrow
the results of the election,

00:06:23.982 --> 00:06:25.751
in part,
because his former client,

00:06:25.751 --> 00:06:27.453
the guy he did all
that dirty work for,

00:06:27.453 --> 00:06:29.388
Donald Trump,
refuses to help him.

00:06:29.388 --> 00:06:31.057
The Daily Beast reported
this week that, even...

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:52.044
Wow, they're not even
acknowledging that it exists.

00:06:52.044 --> 00:06:53.579
Rudy's closest friends
are all treating him

00:06:53.579 --> 00:06:55.581
the way you treat your coworker
when you both get on the subway

00:06:55.581 --> 00:06:56.983
at the same time
and you realize,

00:06:56.983 --> 00:06:58.751
if you start a conversation now,
you're going to have

00:06:58.751 --> 00:07:00.219
to sustain it
for the next 45 minutes.

00:07:00.219 --> 00:07:02.220
In those situations,
I just close my eyes.

00:07:02.220 --> 00:07:03.289
I pretend I'm asleep.

00:07:03.289 --> 00:07:04.790
No wonder Rudy's doing Cameos.

00:07:04.790 --> 00:07:07.560
Soon, he's going to have to pawn
off his precious belongings.

00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:09.695
[ As Biden ]
This is a Yankees
World Series trophy.

00:07:09.695 --> 00:07:11.297
"Sir, that's a Yankee Candle."

00:07:11.297 --> 00:07:13.065
Oh, Rudy!

00:07:13.065 --> 00:07:14.233
You done it again!

00:07:14.233 --> 00:07:16.135
[ Laughter ]
And I'm betting

00:07:16.135 --> 00:07:17.569
an acknowledgment
from Trump would help

00:07:17.569 --> 00:07:20.005
because, I have to say, I follow
Rudy news pretty closely.

00:07:20.005 --> 00:07:23.909
I had no idea -- no idea! --
he had a legal defense fund.

00:07:23.909 --> 00:07:25.077
At this point,
I'm willing to bet

00:07:25.077 --> 00:07:27.512
even Rudy's neighbors
have no idea he has one.

00:07:27.512 --> 00:07:28.714
And I'm just spitballing, here.

00:07:28.714 --> 00:07:29.882
If -- and it's a big if --

00:07:29.882 --> 00:07:31.450
if he lived across the hall
from a guy,

00:07:31.450 --> 00:07:33.018
I don't know, eating a bagel,
in a Yankees hat,

00:07:33.018 --> 00:07:34.687
[ Laughter ]
that guy might say --

00:07:34.687 --> 00:07:36.222
[ As Sandler ]
Oh, so Rudy needs money, huh?

00:07:36.222 --> 00:07:38.057
That makes sense
because, yeah, the other day,

00:07:38.057 --> 00:07:41.093
I saw him trying to stuff
Camel Cash into a parking meter.

00:07:41.093 --> 00:07:43.329
[ Laughter ]
Yeah, he filmed the whole
thing on Cameo.

00:07:43.329 --> 00:07:45.130
Can you believe
this Yankees bullpen?

00:07:45.130 --> 00:07:47.833
How many saves can you blow
in one game?

00:07:47.833 --> 00:07:50.202
[ Laughter ]
What's that?
I know my robe's open.

00:07:50.202 --> 00:07:53.672
[ Laughter ]

00:07:53.672 --> 00:07:55.107
It's a free country.

00:07:55.107 --> 00:07:58.110
Rudy and his allies
have apparently tried

00:07:58.110 --> 00:07:59.411
to get Trump to help,

00:07:59.411 --> 00:08:01.647
either by giving money
to Rudy's legal defense fund

00:08:01.647 --> 00:08:03.548
or, at least,
drawing attention to it,

00:08:03.548 --> 00:08:04.650
but Trump has refused.

00:08:27.139 --> 00:08:29.275
I mean, were you surprised?

00:08:29.275 --> 00:08:31.077
Trump's only drawn to people

00:08:31.077 --> 00:08:32.544
